[narrowed from route-edit-37c339aa] In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.test.ts, replace the entire contents of the file with the test suite given below.

WHY: the current suite has never passed. It fails all four tests with TypeError: undefined is not an object evaluating resolveGapToFeature.gapComposeLastAttemptAt.clear. It was written against an interface that does not exist, in four separate ways. The name is wrong, because the implementation exposes __test__gapComposeLastAttemptAt rather than gapComposeLastAttemptAt. The shape is wrong, because that property is a getter function returning the map, not the map itself. The lifetime is wrong, because the assignment happens inside the resolver body, so the property does not exist until the resolver has been called, while the suite uses it in beforeEach. The arity is wrong, because resolveGapToFeature takes a single pointer argument while the suite passes a second argument as an injected callback that the resolver neither accepts nor invokes. Commit 50fc392 introduced both the test file and that reference together, so the suite has never passed at any point in its history.

WHY THE REPLACEMENT IS CORRECT: requeueAfterNonAttempt is already exported from gap-to-feature.ts with the comment Exported for unit test only, and it takes a fully injectable signature of stamps map, gap id, callback body and an options object carrying nowMs, cooldownMs and requeueMs. The cooldown behaviour can therefore be tested directly and deterministically, with no access to resolver-private state and no injected callback. isNonAttemptComposeResult is exported alongside it. The replacement below was executed against the real module before this goal was written and reported 6 pass, 0 fail, 13 expect calls.

Replace the whole file with exactly this:

import { describe, expect, test } from "bun:test";
import { requeueAfterNonAttempt, isNonAttemptComposeResult } from "./gap-to-feature";

describe("requeueAfterNonAttempt", () => {
  const gapId = "test-gap-id";
  const opts = { nowMs: 1_000_000, cooldownMs: 300_000, requeueMs: 60_000 };

  test("a non-attempt result backdates the stamp so only the requeue window remains", () => {
    const stamps = new Map<string, number>([[gapId, 999_000]]);
    const moved = requeueAfterNonAttempt(stamps, gapId, { verdict: "BUSY" }, opts);
    expect(moved).toBe(true);
    expect(stamps.get(gapId)).toBe(opts.nowMs - (opts.cooldownMs - opts.requeueMs));
  });

  test("a genuine non-landing compose sustains the cooldown", () => {
    const stamps = new Map<string, number>([[gapId, 999_000]]);
    const moved = requeueAfterNonAttempt(stamps, gapId, { verdict: "UNFAVORABLE" }, opts);
    expect(moved).toBe(false);
    expect(stamps.get(gapId)).toBe(999_000);
  });

  test("an unknown gap id is not stamped", () => {
    const stamps = new Map<string, number>();
    expect(requeueAfterNonAttempt(stamps, gapId, { verdict: "BUSY" }, opts)).toBe(false);
    expect(stamps.has(gapId)).toBe(false);
  });

  test("an empty gap id is refused", () => {
    const stamps = new Map<string, number>([["", 999_000]]);
    expect(requeueAfterNonAttempt(stamps, "", { verdict: "BUSY" }, opts)).toBe(false);
  });

  test("a requeue at least as long as the cooldown never extends the exclusion", () => {
    const stamps = new Map<string, number>([[gapId, 999_000]]);
    requeueAfterNonAttempt(stamps, gapId, { stage: "capacity" }, { nowMs: 1_000_000, cooldownMs: 60_000, requeueMs: 300_000 });
    expect(stamps.get(gapId)).toBe(1_000_000);
  });

  test("the non-attempt predicate covers environment, BUSY and capacity", () => {
    expect(isNonAttemptComposeResult({ failure_kind: "environment" })).toBe(true);
    expect(isNonAttemptComposeResult({ verdict: "BUSY" })).toBe(true);
    expect(isNonAttemptComposeResult({ stage: "capacity" })).toBe(true);
    expect(isNonAttemptComposeResult({ verdict: "UNFAVORABLE" })).toBe(false);
    expect(isNonAttemptComposeResult(null)).toBe(false);
  });
});

